  "notes": "ゆらゆら is an onomatopoeic (mimetic) word describing slow, gentle, rhythmic swaying or wavering motion.\n\nUSAGE:\n- As adverb: ゆらゆら{揺|ゆ}れる (to sway gently)\n- With する: ゆらゆらする (to be swaying)\n- With と: ゆらゆらと (more literary)\n\nTYPICAL SUBJECTS:\n- {炎|ほのお}がゆらゆら: flames flickering\n- {船|ふね}がゆらゆら: boat rocking gently\n- {影|かげ}がゆらゆら: shadows wavering\n- {水草|みずくさ}がゆらゆら: water plants swaying\n\nRELATED:\n{揺|ゆ}れる (to shake/sway) is the related verb. ゆらゆら emphasizes the slow, gentle, back-and-forth quality of the motion.",
